            "result_text": "Done! The regex has been saved to `/app/regex.txt`.\n\nHere's how it works:\n\n**IPv4 Validation**: Each octet allows 0-255 without leading zeros:\n- `0` (single zero)\n- `1-9` (single digit)\n- `10-99` (two digits)\n- `100-199`, `200-249`, `250-255` (three digits with proper ranges)\n\n**Date Validation**: Month-specific day ranges:\n- Months 01,03,05,07,08,10,12: days 01-31\n- Months 04,06,09,11: days 01-30  \n- Month 02: days 01-29\n\n**Last Date Matching**:\n- `(?=.*IPv4)` ensures the line contains an IPv4\n- `.*?` matches non-greedily to find the date\n- Captured date has word boundaries (`\\b`) to exclude false matches\n- `(?!.*date_pattern)` negative lookahead ensures no more dates follow on the line\n\nThe regex respects MULTILINE mode where `.` stays within single lines, so the search doesn't cross line boundaries."
